node_modules/
# Build output. `dist*/` rather than `dist/` on purpose: the build flow renames
# dist out of the way before rebuilding (vite's emptyOutDir trips the Windows
# safe-delete guard on large trees), which leaves a `dist.stale-NNN/` directory
# behind. Listing only `dist/` let 202 KaTeX font/asset files get committed that
# way once.
dist*/
target/
# Shipped installers. Deliberately OUTSIDE dist/: tauri.conf.json embeds all of
# dist/ into the binary, so an installer kept there gets nested into the next one.
release/
*.local
.DS_Store
public/cmaps/
public/standard_fonts/

# Browser profiles. NEVER commit these.
#
# The CDP experiments used `--user-data-dir` inside evidence/, and those
# directories accumulated real profile data: Cookies, History, Web Data and a
# `Login Data` holding 267 saved-credential rows, plus the `Local State` file
# with the key material that protects them. 1477 such files were committed once.
# A fresh Edge profile has zero rows in all of those, so this was never filler.
#
# The catch-all is deliberate: a specific list is what let edge-serve-profile
# slip through while edge-ctrl-profile was covered.
*-profile/
**/*-profile/
Login Data
Cookies
Web Data
Local State
